Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:01.52,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1296)}But the Sunnah is that wear\Nthe
Dialogue: 0,0:00:01.52,0:00:03.05,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1296)}ring on your small finger.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.05,0:00:04.57,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1296)}As for the first finger,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.57,0:00:06.10,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1296)}the second
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.10,0:00:07.53,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1296)}finger, and the ring finger,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.53,0:00:08.96,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1296)}the ulama prohibit it.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.96,0:00:10.39,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1296)}And there are reports\Nregarding that from
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.39,0:00:11.82,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1296)}the
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.82,0:00:13.45,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1296)}Sunnah too, especially for\Nthe first finger
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.45,0:00:15.07,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1296)}and the middle finger.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.07,0:00:16.70,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1296)}The ring finger,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.92,0:00:20.12,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1296)}that's a prohibition from the\Nscholars because
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.12,0:00:23.32,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1296)}they connect it to At-Tasha\NBuhubi Kufar,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.56,0:00:26.15,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1296)}behaving like Kufar, who\Nchoose wearing rings
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.15,0:00:28.75,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1296)}to be on the ring finger,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.75,0:00:31.34,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1296)}because they believe that
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.88,0:00:33.87,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1296)}that connects the heart from\Nthat finger.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.87,0:00:35.85,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1296)}So when you put a ring on
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.85,0:00:37.84,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1296)}it during marriage,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.46,0:00:40.16,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1296)}the ring helps you to sustain\Nyour
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.16,0:00:41.86,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1296)}marriage. So we avoid that.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.86,0:00:43.56,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1296)}They do it for worship.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:43.56,0:00:45.26,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1296)}We avoid
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.26,0:00:47.25,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1296)}behaving like them. So that\Nwho sees
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.25,0:00:49.23,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1296)}us does not think that we\Nalso
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.23,0:00:51.22,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1296)}have that belief they have.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.34,0:00:53.83,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1296)}So don't put rings on your\Nfirst
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.83,0:00:55.31,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1296)}three fingers, the first\Nfinger,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.31,0:00:56.80,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1296)}the middle finger,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.80,0:00:58.20,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1296)}and the ring finger.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:58.20,0:00:59.59,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1296)}You can put your ring on the
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.59,0:01:00.99,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1296)}thumb, but the Sunnah is that\Nyou
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.99,0:01:02.38,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1296)}have your ring
Dialogue: 0,0:01:02.38,0:01:04.30,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1296)}on the small finger.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.30,0:01:06.21,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1296)}For men, as for women,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.21,0:01:08.13,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1296)}put the ring wherever you\Nwant.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:08.13,0:01:10.04,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1296)}If you like,

